    "doc": "mk37.pdf",
    "page": "4 and 5",
    "section": "Ordering Schematic"
  },
  "note": "Extracted by hand from the ordering schematic, model dash size dash body then a slash. The seat Cv column splits between the 37 and the equal percentage 377, and the shared digits mean different flows on each side, 2 is 0.42 or 80 and 3 is 0.84 or 230, so the labels carry both readings and the exclusive codes refuse the other model, the Mark 70 device. The range and actuator columns carry the sheet's consult-factory line for 2-1/2 to 6 inch, held as a caution on those sizes rather than a refusal, since the codes themselves print unbanded. The trim splits by signal, the on-off trims with the on-off range and the mA and volt trims with the signal ranges, per the trims' own labels. The accessories column prints no none row, held for the PDF.",
